blender-web — licensing summary
===============================

The blender-web project, as an aggregate, is licensed under the
GNU General Public License, version 3 or later (GPL-3.0-or-later).

Individual files are licensed under the terms named in their own
SPDX-License-Identifier header. Files derived from Blender carry
GPL-2.0-or-later (or their true upstream license — for example Apache-2.0
for Cycles-derived code); new web-port files follow the same terms.

Full license texts live in the LICENSES/ directory:
  - LICENSES/GPL-2.0-or-later.txt
  - LICENSES/GPL-3.0-or-later.txt
  - LICENSES/CC0-1.0.txt      (project data: ledger, notes, reports)

Provenance for every derived module is recorded in PROVENANCE.md.
Third-party runtime dependencies and their licenses are listed in
THIRD-PARTY.md. Attribution and trademark notices are in NOTICE.

The preferred form for making modifications is this source repository
(GPLv3 section 6(d)); the application footer links "Source code (GPL)" to it.

This project is source-derived from Blender (https://www.blender.org) and is
not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by the Blender Foundation.
Blender(R) is a registered trademark of the Blender Foundation.
